  "description": "<p>Alexander College is a private post-secondary institution in Burnaby, British Columbia, Canada, The establishment offers courses at the undergraduate level. Options for University Transfer, Associate of Arts degree and Associate of Science degree are also available. The college currently specialises in several subject areas including, Economics, Computer Science, Psychology, Business and Mathematics.</p><p>As classes are small in number, students receive high-quality learning opportunities in a supportive environment. Furthermore, individual growth and development are encouraged through academia and wider community engagement.</p> <p>In September 2021, Alexander opened its new campus in Burnaby. Here, students have access to state-of-the-art classrooms, laboratories and communal student spaces. The new campus also has a comfortable library where students will find all the necessary books, databases and IT facilities to complete courses. An affordable bookshop is also on-campus to help students find appropriate learning materials.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>With a diverse and supportive learning environment, students from different backgrounds are welcomed warmly at Alexander College. Upon arrival, students can join the orienteering tour on campus and meet like-minded coursemates and teaching staff. The student union also has many extracurricular events and clubs to join. These include dance classes, athletics clubs, sports teams and cultural and social organisations.</p>",
